---
source: crates/modde-cli/tests/cli_help_snapshots.rs
expression: "stdout(&[\"profile\", \"--help\"])"
---
Manage profiles

Usage: modde profile [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  list        List all profiles
  switch      Switch to a profile (swaps saves automatically)
  create      Create a new profile
  delete      Delete a profile
  try         Experiment with a profile (can be stacked, like git branches)
  rollback    Roll back to the previous profile (undo the last `try`)
  commit      Accept the current experiment, clearing the rollback stack
  active      Show the active profile for a game
  fork        Fork a profile (clone mods + saves into a new profile)
  lock        Apply a manual profile-level load order lock
  unlock      Clear the profile-level load order lock
  lock-info   Show lock status for a profile
  lock-mod    Pin an individual mod in place (per-mod lock)
  unlock-mod  Release an individual mod's per-mod pin
  dedup       Detect (and optionally remove) filesystem-scanner rows in a profile that duplicate mods the Wabbajack manifest already installs. See `plans/greedy-shimmying-pine.md` for background
  help        Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --data-dir <DATA_DIR>          Override data directory (default: ~/.local/share/modde or $`MODDE_DATA_DIR`) [env: MODDE_DATA_DIR=]
      --config-dir <CONFIG_DIR>      Override the base configuration directory used by modde and its session journal
      --heap-profile <HEAP_PROFILE>  Write a DHAT heap profile. Requires the `heap-profile` cargo feature [env: MODDE_HEAP_PROFILE=]
  -h, --help                         Print help
